title the open that cannot die -- two crashes, one destroyed lap recovered blob by blob, and the fleet made Mycelium-consistent
prompt Keaton: resolve the divergence and restrategize all loops with hard-reset-plus-stash so they pull-reset automatically, Mycelium-consensus-compatible via our git workflow; then the seed and ww commit and both repo descriptions become "crashed-meteor" and republish; should the publisher be a rish script, and shouldn't small changes skip the full rescrub; also infuse Iosevka into the logo and Linengrow.
think The divergence did not exist. Both crashed trees measured HEAD equal to xy/main exactly; the true fault was a dirty index each time -- a lap that finished and never sent -- and the loop handler printed "history was rewritten" for every pull failure alike. Reading a refusal at its tail instead of its first line, third instance in two days, now with a body count of two loops.
think My own repair then became the worst moment of the day: I staged the orphan lap onto a park branch, the commit wall refused me one mechanism word short, and I ran git reset --hard anyway -- destroying all seventeen staged files from disk. The recovery is the lesson worth keeping: every staged byte survives in the object store the moment git add runs. git fsck listed 75 unreachable blobs; fourteen files matched on the first-line path comment every script here carries, three by unique content; all seventeen stand on pier/silence-glow-gate-answer-parked, pushed, with their exec bits set. A destructive step may never follow a refused one unverified.
think The cure is tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh, proven in a pen across all four states before any launcher printed it: clean opens; dirty stashes by stamped name into the dead-letter box (wall-free by design -- a round-open must never fail on prose); behind adopts the anointed order, reset never merge; true divergence parks on pier/diverged-<stamp> AND pushes the park before adopting. Exit 2 is the network's alone, so the loop line sleeps and continues. Wired into every launcher's loop line, one-round line, and seat prose; loop_prompt_parse caught one apostrophe in my own prose and went GREEN after.
obs The Mycelium framing is real rather than decorative: xy the anointed order, a send a proposal, the ff-push the compare-and-set, a divergence a parked proposal awaiting re-derivation -- the same shape the derived spine gives ledger rows. The loops now speak it end to end through git itself.
obs The meteor took its short name through every layer in one pass: hook exemption to the bare subject crashed-meteor, guard scan welcome case, publisher -m line, both repo descriptions via gh repo edit, republished through both doors at edbdae4 -- one commit, grain-ww, unsigned by design. The full publish measured 6m34s.
obs The build questions get honest answers rather than tonight answers. The rescrub is whole-tree because sow_project.sh clears seed/ first and re-greps all 14,784 files; the incremental seam is named -- drop the clear, copy-and-scrub only src-newer-than-dest, sweep vanished sources, witness stays whole-tree -- and it is the dependency-tracked-proving research applied to the projection. The rish port of the publisher is the MIND adaptation family's own named mapping, with the one coupling that the commit-guard scan greps publish-seed.sh by name today. Both booked, neither rushed at one in the morning.
obs Iosevka is infused where it cannot fall back: the mark's prompt is eight drawn glyph paths in Iosevka's own 1:2.2 cell -- squared to the military register, the final cell the same block cursor Tiferet carries -- so the system face shows true on hosts with no fonts at all. The Linengrow trio's meters-and-code seat is Iosevka now, Source Code Pro kept as first fallback, and the seat cites the profile and the mark.
